From adacc64dcd1325f7a81c6f8fc55086eac98fc7bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claudius <claudiusthebot@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:47:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: gts7xlwifi: allow setting the PMIC RTC
 (optional)

The PM8150 RTC counter keeps counting while the tablet is off, but it
starts from an arbitrary value (reads 1970) and the driver refuses to
write it without allow-set-time. Samsung's DT does not set it either;
Android keeps its own offset on top of the counter.

No SM8250 board in mainline sets allow-set-time, so whether the SPMI
arbiter gives the apps EE write access to the RTC peripheral (0x60) on
this tablet is untested. If it does not, spmi-pmic-arb rejects the write
with -EPERM ("disallowed SPMI write") before it reaches the PMIC.

With write access, the kernel's 11-minute mode (RTC_SYSTOHC) and
'hwclock -w' store NTP time in the counter, and it survives reboots
without the userspace offset. Android/TWRP would then see a different
counter until they resync from the network.

Optional: not applied by the CI build (lives in linux-patches/optional).
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-gts7xlwifi.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-gts7xlwifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-gts7xlwifi.dts
index e81c8f1a4..30501a902 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-gts7xlwifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-gts7xlwifi.dts
@@ -1027,6 +1027,17 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The PM8150 RTC counter runs while the tablet is off. Samsung's DT keeps it
+ * read-only (Android adds an offset); allow writing it so that NTP time
+ * (kernel 11-minute mode, hwclock -w) survives a reboot. If the SPMI arbiter
+ * does not grant this EE write access, the write fails with -EPERM and
+ * nothing changes.
+ */
+&{/soc@0/spmi@c440000/pmic@0/rtc@6000} {
+	allow-set-time;
+};
+
 &pm8150l_adc {
 	channel@4d {
 		reg = <ADC5_AMUX_THM1_100K_PU>;
-- 
2.43.0

